<title>USA: Fed's Moskow speaks to price stability goal.</title>
<headline>Fed's Moskow speaks to price stability goal.</headline>
<dateline>DANA POINT, Calif. 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Federal Reserve Bank President Michael Moskow said on Thursday that price stability will be evident when inflation does not factor in to consumer or business decisions.</p>
<p>When Moskow was asked how price stability will be evident when it is reached, he replied: &quot;When inflation does not interfere with the actions of consumers and business.&quot;</p>
<p>Moskow was responding to reporters' questions following a speech delivered here.</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1600))</p>
</text>
